# Text files are LF in the index and on every checkout, as they were in
# economicspace, whose `*.py` / `*.md` rules did not come with the move: without
# them a Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true by default) checked them out CRLF.
*.py           text eol=lf
*.md           text eol=lf
LICENSE        text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Archival data committed verbatim.  `sdsstax_ast.tab` is a PDS3 fixed-width
# table from the NASA Planetary Data System, and it arrives CRLF.  Marking it
# -text means git never converts it, on any host: the bytes that were
# downloaded are the bytes that are checked out, and a mechanically rewritten
# archive file is no longer the artefact its citation names.  See CITATIONS.md.
*.tab -text
